  "verdict": "CENTRE-BIAS CONFIRMED AND QUANTIFIED; H1's RELATIVE VERDICT HOLDS OFF-CENTRE. The trivial centre-prior baseline scores 22/22 (1.00) under the centred window used by every localization run to date, and 0/22 (0.00) once the transition is moved off-centre -- a drop of 1.00 (>= 0.30, so the inflation \u00a72b warns about is real). So the ABSOLUTE localization hit rates reported across the suite were inflated by the symmetric-window construction and should be read as such. With the transition off-centre, the manifold-vs-scalar comparison is manifold 10/22 vs scalar 10/22 (McNemar manifold-only 5, scalar-only 5, p = 1.000): the manifold is still not certified superior (nor inferior), so H1's INCONCLUSIVE verdict is robust to the confound -- the paired comparison was not an artefact of the centre prior. Not a power increase: n is unchanged from H1 (PhysioNet unreachable this session).",
